  "notes": "Times in seconds of the cut. Targets are logical names the runner maps to app selectors. Actions: rest, hover, walk, click, demo, slider (drag a track from `from` to `to`; `editor-hue` runs 0-360 and starts from the current hue when `from` is omitted), box (drag the color editor's saturation/brightness handle to `[s, b]`), tip (drag the hex tip by hue degrees; with `via: \"hue-label\"` the cursor holds the hue pill by its outer rim instead (the control keeps the pointer on the pill's radial line, so a corner grip is not possible) and takes it round the ring), orbit (drag the tip around the field with wobble), stem (drag one channel stem in or out), rect (drag a solid red marquee around a target from a corner; the travel to the first corner is inside `ms`; holds `hold` ms then fades; cut short, it snaps to full size; with `hands: \"free\"` it draws itself without the cursor, so it can run over a drag), circle (a ring that draws itself around a target over `ms` without the cursor, so it can share an `at` with a hover; same hold), loop (hover circuit), wander (curved playful move to a target), underline (move to just under a link's left end and sweep to its right end over `ms`, resting there), color (tween), scroll, leave. Revision 4 from Taylor's review of revision 3, 2026-09-10: 4.1 hue turned by the hue label, 5.2 marquee on the RGB values while the saturation drops, 10.3 color back to the default, 10.5 the author link underlined and the cursor left there.",
